# .gitignore — Rishwanth's job-application workflow repo
#
# This repo holds only the four job-application skills: cv-tailoring,
# cover-letter, jd-recruiter-brief, application-qa. They are copied here from
# the Claude app's skills folder by sync-and-commit.sh — see GIT_WORKFLOW.md.
#
# Anthropic's bundled skills (docx, pdf, pptx, xlsx, skill-creator, morning,
# schedule, setup-cowork, consolidate-memory, explain-usage) live alongside
# these in the app folder but are deliberately NOT copied here: they are not
# Rishwanth's content, they are updated by app syncs rather than by the
# change_protocol, and they would add ~208 files (mostly OOXML .xsd schemas)
# that would bury real workflow diffs in `git log`. They are excluded by the
# sync script, so they need no rule here.
#
# Everything below is either regenerated output or machine noise. None of it
# belongs in a log meant to read as a provenance audit trail.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode caches — regenerated on every run of validate.py,
# build_bank.py and build_index.py. Tracking them would produce a diff on
# every validation run, which is not a workflow change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / distribution output — packaged skill bundles (e.g. from
# skill-creator's package_skill.py) and archives of this tree. All derived
# from tracked sources, so never the source of truth for a fact or a rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
*.zip
*.tar.gz


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated per-application documents — tailored CVs and cover letters
# produced for a specific job. These are outputs, not system state. The three
# master CVs under cv-tailoring/assets/ ARE tracked, because they are inputs.
# Delete these rules if you later decide to version submitted applications.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/output/
/applications/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS Finder metadata — written into any browsed folder. Excluded by the
# sync script too, belt and braces. Never content.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor scratch files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files Claude chats save next to the repo (not skill content).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Claude outputs/
